WEBVTT

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.250
Darkest Peru.

00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:41.500
A vast, unexplored wilderness
shrouded in mystery. Until now!

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:44.708
For I have been charged
by my fellow geographers

00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:47.083
to leave the comforts
of home and family

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:50.542
and set off upon
a voyage of discovery.

00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:56.125
I travel light, carrying only
the absolute essentials.

00:00:56.208 --> 00:00:59.208
Maps, rations, modest timepiece
and travel piano.

00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:05.333
And finally, deep in the undergrowth,
I spot something extraordinary.

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:09.542
An undiscovered species of bear.

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:12.417
Time to collect a specimen
for the museum.

00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:20.375
I thought my time was up,
my ticket was punched.

00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:23.625
But the bear saved my life.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.750
He guided me through the jungle
to show me his world,

00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:30.042
and in return,
I introduced him to ours.

00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:34.250
That's, enn... That's a telescope.
That's my grandfather's telescope.

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:37.417
Oh, be very careful with that.

00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:40.625
That's soap. Really wouldn't eat that.

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:45.167
Here we are, why don't you try this?
This is marmalade.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.542
You spread it on toast,
put it in sandwiches, or...

00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:51.875
Or you can drink it. Jolly good.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.167
This is London. That's where I'm from.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.500
Lon-don.

00:01:58.208 --> 00:02:00.417
Good Lord!

00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:02.792
Now try Stratford-upon-Avon.

00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:06.125
Over time, I become friends
with the bears and even name them.

00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:08.792
The female after
my dear departed mother

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:12.208
and the male after an exotic boxer
I once met in a bar.

00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:15.333
But the time eventually comes
to return to my wife and daughter

00:02:15.417 --> 00:02:17.208
and share my findings with the world.

00:02:17.292 --> 00:02:20.000
Goodbye, Lucy. Goodbye, Pastuzo.

00:02:20.125 --> 00:02:24.667
And if you ever make it to London,
you can be sure of a very warm welcome.

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.542
I have learnt so much from these bears

00:02:26.625 --> 00:02:31.083
but I wonder what, if anything,
they have learnt from me.

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:44.625
Marmalade!

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:50.250
They're ripe. They're ripe.
They're finally ripe!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.208
Aunt Lucy!

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:54.125
Uncle Pastuzo!

00:02:54.208 --> 00:02:57.250
You're never going to guess... Whoa!

00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:05.500
Good morning, Aunt Lucy.

00:03:05.708 --> 00:03:07.625
Good morning, my little hurricane.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.000
Why do you have to come crashing in here
like a natural disaster?

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:15.542
But, Uncle Pastuzo... they're ripe.

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:19.208
Whoa-ho-ho!

00:03:19.292 --> 00:03:21.125
It's Marmalade Day!

00:03:21.208 --> 00:03:22.792
Marmalade Day!

00:03:24.292 --> 00:03:26.750
Oh, it rather suits me. Marmalade Day!

00:03:27.458 --> 00:03:30.125
Oh, do calm down, you two.

00:03:30.208 --> 00:03:32.417
There's no need to rush.

00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:37.958
Now be careful up there.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.250
And keep your paws off my hat.

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:42.792
I will.

00:03:57.542 --> 00:03:58.917
Marmalade.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.167
Just one sandwich contains
all the vitamins and minerals

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.000
a bear needs for a whole day.

00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:08.208
- Amazing.
- Hmm.

00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:12.667
And your Aunt Lucy's recipe
is even better than the explorer's.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.875
We must remember to take him a jar
when we go to London.

00:04:15.958 --> 00:04:17.292
London?

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:21.708
I wouldn't worry! We've been talking
about that trip for 40 years.

00:04:21.792 --> 00:04:23.750
One day, Pastuzo.

00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:25.625
But why would you want to go anywhere

00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:27.708
when we live in
the best place in the world?

00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:30.542
Whoa!

00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:34.708
Whoa-hum

00:04:36.833 --> 00:04:37.875
Goodness.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.292
I thought I told you to be careful.

00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:43.792
And give me back my hat.

00:04:43.875 --> 00:04:45.917
- Yes, Uncle. But...
- No buts.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.042
It's about time I got a bit of respect
around here.

00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:53.042
Embarrassing.

00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:55.500
But tasty.

00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:03.417
Friendly advice for the foreigner
in London. Lesson three.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.917
It's dusk, and you pass a stranger
in the street.

00:05:07.042 --> 00:05:09.208
- Greet them politely.
- Good evening.

00:05:09.292 --> 00:05:12.125
To take the conversation further,
talk about the weather.

00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:14.292
Real brolly-buster, isn't it?

00:05:14.333 --> 00:05:18.417
Fact; Londoners have 101 ways
to say that it is raining...

00:05:18.458 --> 00:05:22.083
- Can I have the last sandwich?
- Oh, no, I need that.

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:25.208
A wise bear always keeps
a marmalade sandwich in his hat

00:05:25.292 --> 00:05:27.042
in case of emergency.

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:29.125
And it's bucketing down.

00:05:29.208 --> 00:05:33.792
Follow these simple rules and you will
always feel at home in London.

00:05:41.125 --> 00:05:43.125
- Aunt Lucy?
- Earthquake!

00:05:44.833 --> 00:05:46.667
Get to the shelter!

00:05:58.208 --> 00:05:59.667
Oh!

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.167
- Aunt Lucy!
- Keep going!

00:06:06.042 --> 00:06:07.542
Are you alright?

00:06:21.125 --> 00:06:22.208
Uncle Pastuzo!

00:06:23.375 --> 00:06:24.417
Uncle Pastuzo!

00:06:25.208 --> 00:06:26.417
Get down!

00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:45.125
Uncle Pastuzo?

00:06:48.333 --> 00:06:49.667
Pastuzo?

00:06:54.292 --> 00:06:56.458
Uncle Pastuzo?

00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:06.375
Aunt Lucy.

